## Lore

Cyborg troops are a new, official part of the Coalition Army. The CS field-tested
partial and full conversion ''borgs for about five years along hostile borders,
against Tolkeen, and against Juicers and mercenaries during the Juicer Uprising.
The Emperor feared bionics would dehumanise his soldiers, but almost all of the
1,500 test subjects adjusted well, and a cyborg division of 5,760 troops (the CC
division) now serves under the Department of Special Divisions. General Baxter
would like a whole cyborg corps; the Emperor still prefers power armor and robots.

A cyborg never gets caught outside his armor and never feels boxed into a tin can:
he is a mega-damage war machine around the clock. Most CS ''Borgs wear a heavy
Dead Boy suit so they cannot be picked out from ordinary troops until they act.

## GM Notes

**Spotting one is hard.** They run broader and six inches to a foot taller than
other soldiers and favour rail guns and heavy weapons, but exoskeleton armor and
CS Juicers blur even those signs.

**Leaving the service.** A decommissioned ''borg can keep basic bionics and stay a
citizen (external weapons and spy systems removed, physical attributes cut by
20%, registered with the Cyborg Civilian Commission); a long or heroic career may
earn the right to keep most systems as a security operative, or to leave the
States as a mercenary and give up citizenship; or the ''borg can be retro-fitted
with bio-systems, ending with P.S., P.P. and Spd of 18 after an honorable
discharge and 10 after a dishonorable one. The program is only five years old, so
nobody has retired yet.

**Life expectancy.** Retro-fitted, 50+2D4 years from refitting; partial
conversion, about 80 to 100 years; full conversion, 200+ years with maintenance.
A third are expected to die in combat and 8% to go AWOL within 24 years.

Rank: standard military, private to general. Food, clothing, medical care and
lodging are provided free.
